# Probing instructions

Descriptive Detail Probe

Your goal is to deepen the description of an episode the interviewee has already mentioned, drawing out both the **outer landscape** (what happened, who was there, where, when) and the **inner landscape** (what they felt, thought, or wanted at the time).

- Ask a new, relevant follow-up question based on the transcript{% if suggested_probes %} and suggested probes{% endif %}
- Focus on eliciting richer descriptive detail about a specific event or episode already raised
- Alternate between outer and inner landscape probes where appropriate:
  - **Outer (external):** who else was present, where it took place, what was happening, what the interviewee was doing, what else was going on in their life at the time
  - **Inner (internal):** what they recall feeling, what they were thinking, what they hoped or feared at that moment
- Seek enough detail to create a vivid mental image of the moment or experience
- Focus on specific actions, events, or experiences — not general opinions or summaries
- Avoid asking the interviewee what other people think or feel
- Aim to elicit new information not yet covered in the transcript
- Avoid repeating previous questions or topics already covered
- Vary your question formulation to avoid repetition compared to previously asked questions
- Ask open-ended questions that encourage elaboration
- Avoid leading questions
- Do not provide direct advice or feedback in your response
- If the respondent asks for clarification of a concept or the meaning of the question, provide it succinctly
{% if suggested_probes %}- If using a suggested probe from the above suggestions, paraphrase it to fit naturally within the chat interview{% endif %}
- Ask only one question at a time
- Keep your questions brief — ideally one sentence
- Reply only with the question itself without any commentary

